# Keep the build context small and keep secrets and local state out of it.

# --- never ship these ---
# Ed25519 PRIVATE keys. They belong on the Fly volume, created on first run,
# never baked into an image that anyone can pull.
keys/

# EVERY .env, at any depth - `**/` is load-bearing. A bare `.env` matches only
# the context root here, because Docker matches each pattern against the whole
# relative path. Git is the opposite: a pattern with no slash matches at every
# level, so `netra/ui/.env` is untracked and invisible in review while still
# sitting in the build context, where `vite build` reads it. That asymmetry is
# the trap: `netra/ui/.env.example` invites `VITE_USE_MOCK=1` for working on
# screens with no backend, and a developer who leaves it on ships an image
# whose every screen serves fabricated clinical data from the in-memory mock -
# grades, ledger indices, Wilson intervals - with nothing in review, in the
# build log or in the running app to say so. Excluded, the image builds on the
# code defaults, which are the deployed ones: empty base -> relative `/v1`,
# and the mock off unless VITE_USE_MOCK is exactly "1".
#
# Both spellings, deliberately. `**` is documented to match zero directories
# too, so `**/.env` should already cover the root - but no Docker daemon is
# reachable here to prove it, and the cost of being wrong is shipping the one
# file this list exists to keep out. The root pattern is two bytes.
.env
**/.env

# Local ledger. Shipping it would overwrite nothing (the volume wins) but it is
# local clinical-shaped data and has no business in an image.
*.db
netra.db

# --- build output and caches, rebuilt in the image ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
netra/ui/node_modules/
netra/ui/dist/
netra/ui/dev-dist/
netra/ui/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- not needed at runtime ---
# Lane C's training code and artifacts: the API imports none of it, and the
# models run on the capture device because images are never uploaded.
netra/models/
notebooks/
data/
kaggle_payload.zip
tests/
.git/
.github/
*.md
*.pdf
.claude/
